mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Critical Care Medicine is a vital branch of clinical medicine focused on life support, multi-organ function monitoring, and treatment for critically ill patients. This course is designed for medical undergraduates, graduate students, resident physicians, and ICU specialist healthcare providers. It systematically explains the pathophysiological mechanisms, treatment principles, and advanced technologies for managing critically ill patients, aiming to cultivate students' clinical thinking and practical skills in acute and critical care scenarios.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
